id: pm-gh1091
title: "GH-1091: surface extension manifest schema lint separately from version compatibility"
description: "GitHub issue #1091 reports that manifest_unknown_key is only reachable through an SDK analyzer, is absent from pm health and package/extension discovery, and shares one findings array with version compatibility verdicts, making exact compatibility assertions unstable across CLI upgrades."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[5]: "area:extensions","area:sdk",diagnostics,manifest-schema,package-platform
created_at: "2026-08-22T18:40:17.079Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-25T10:02:33.270Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-25T09:51:10.197Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-25T09:51:10.197Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 240
acceptance_criteria: pm health surfaces unknown manifest keys with actionable author guidance; public SDK exposes a stable schema-lint boundary or separates schema findings from compatibility verdicts; extension/package listings preserve thin-adapter parity; docs identify the supported author-metadata location; focused SDK CLI MCP tests and exact full coverage pass
parent: pm-usfg
risk: medium
confidence: high
severity: medium
environment: pm-cli 2026.8.21 extension manifest authoring and health surfaces
repro_steps: "Add an ignored top-level manifest key such as pm; run pm health, context, extension list, and package list; compare their silence with checkExtensionManifestCompatibility findings."
resolution: Stable public schema lint and shared author-workspace diagnostics now distinguish manifest advisories from version compatibility and surface them through health and doctor transports.
expected_result: "CLI health/discovery exposes ignored manifest keys, and the public SDK offers a stable separation between schema lint and version-compatibility verdicts."
actual_result: "Only checkExtensionManifestCompatibility exposes manifest_unknown_key, and its flat findings array mixes schema advisories with compatibility failures."
customer_impact: Extension authors ship inert keys without diagnostics and exact compatibility assertions break when new advisory schema codes are added.
